{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_f17a0913b965f55054c26537f8bfb90292ed717f3cdd8f086a3c0768b2c14686", "title": "Electronic Arts", "text": "Electronic Arts Inc. (EA) is an American video game company headquartered in Redwood City, California. Founded and incorporated on May 28, 1982 by Trip Hawkins, the company was a pioneer of the early home computer games industry and was notable for promoting the designers and programmers responsible for its games. As of September 2017, Electronic Arts is the second-largest gaming company in the Americas and Europe by revenue and market capitalization after Activision Blizzard and ahead of Take-Two Interactive.", "score": 18.0061}, {"id": "hp_doc_ec6684140201788b38d1f4ade7695611e69c6fcd7f46c365fa032bd5f425bfaa", "title": "Legacy of the Ancients", "text": "Legacy of the Ancients is a fantasy role-playing video game published by Electronic Arts in 1987.", "score": 13.2236}, {"id": "hp_doc_7f57a5cf8fdcb0a44bd8049a8f4c7164a218093471e1a36c01dd5f4f34c3259a", "title": "Australian Ballet School", "text": "The Australian Ballet School was founded in 1964 as the primary training facility for The Australian Ballet by Dame Margaret Scott. It is part of the Australian Ballet Centre, which is located in the Melbourne Arts Precinct, Southbank in Melbourne, Victoria. It is a member of the Australian Roundtable for Arts Training Excellence.", "score": 10.2619}], "remaining_searches": 1}
